@page "/privacy/receipt-importer"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Receipt importer privacy policy - Group Split</PageTitle>

<article class="gs-receipt-privacy">
    <a href="/">Group Split</a>
    <h1>Receipt importer privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 3, 2026</p>
    <p>The GroupSplit receipt importer helps you import selected purchases from Amazon and Costco into your GroupSplit receipts inbox using Microsoft Edge. You choose when to connect a store and start an import.</p>

    <h2>Information the importer uses</h2>
    <p>For Amazon, the importer reads order dates and ship-to names for the optional recipient filter. It verifies the order number on the printable receipt and saves the full page as a PDF. The PDF may include customer names, addresses, payment details and order numbers. Review the printable receipt before importing.</p>
    <p>For Costco warehouse purchases, the importer reads receipt listings and prints the displayed receipt to PDF. A Costco receipt may include customer or membership information and masked payment details. For Costco online purchases, the importer generates a summary from the order date, items, quantities, prices and totals.</p>
    <p>You sign in directly to the retailer. The extension uses your existing browser session and does not ask for or store your retailer password.</p>

    <h2>Where information goes</h2>
    <p>When you choose to save and import receipts, the extension saves a PDF copy in your Downloads/GroupSplit folder and uploads it to your signed-in GroupSplit inbox. GroupSplit reads new attachments to suggest receipt details and stores uploaded receipts under your account.</p>
    <p>The extension does not configure analytics or send retailer data to an additional third-party service. Retailers and Microsoft Edge handle their own requests under their respective policies.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You decide which retailer to connect and when to start an import. You can review results before importing, delete downloaded copies from your device, and remove receipts from GroupSplit. You can also remove the extension or revoke its site permissions in Microsoft Edge.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests about your GroupSplit data, sign in and use the <a href="/help">GroupSplit help page</a>. Please do not include passwords or payment details in a support request.</p>
</article>

